test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T09:11:19.2747233Z             "body": "Preserves original Playwright MCP tools while adding the bounded local batch/jobs companion. Publishing remains disabled. **Draft; mission incomplete, no merge/release requested.**\n\nNew source-test fix: the original client fixture accumulated stderr without a limit. A real MCP child emitting1,048,577 bytes before initialize was accepted with1,048,742 bytes retained. The fixture now retains at most1MiB, grows from small storage, continues draining after overflow, rejects truncated reads with a fixed error, awaits every existing client close and fails if stderr EOF is unconfirmed. No extra cleanup wait/timer/kill, product transport policy, workflow field or default changed. Negative overflow returns expected exit1 without canary text. Source-only helpers/preload are excluded from the runtime tarball.\n\nLocal final verification: helper/reporter9/9 eachNode20/22/24;14 Chromium/Firefox regressions (12 browser cases plus2 protocol-only), full Node20/22 protocol1/1 each; Chrome/WebKit-configured protocol1/1 each without engine launch. Local WebKit engine remains unexecuted. Fresh176-file production install passes; the extra file versus native80 is RELEASE_BLOCKERS.md, not QA code. Lint, syntax, actionlint and diff checks pass; ShellCheck/Pyflakes are not run. Before/intermediate/final source hashes and individual outcomes are retained in native81-stderr-proof.json. Native82 is running at `bbf4764e001095d42aecaa7e3ce671fb21fa568d`: [Batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39748755708), [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39748755718). Pending is not PASS.\n\nLatest completed native81 at `93da4be7034effa08a280fd877ef12c1f34e2f6a`: **1,904 reported test passes / 9 failures**, plus Mac actual-Codex TIMED_OUT994 and a failed Windows protocol-headed JSON control. [Batch](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39743244640):1,446/6; [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39743244612):458/3. Both fail;17 non-soak jobs conclude, optional soak skips, reported test skips/cancellations0. This documentation-only head predates the new stderr fix.\n\nFive176-file installs, all journal lanes112/113,15 action/HTTP/cancellation cases each and five raw/supervised20-run fixtures pass. Remaining native failures: Mac SDK995/synchronous991/actual994 deadlines; three Windows raw Firefox input/close failures; later fragment retry-case lifecycle timeout after429/503 passed; Windows legacy eighth run all23 then server-close timeout; Mac Chrome screenshot protocol error and Firefox storage case's30s deadline while restore is pending. Target-closed during teardown is not evidence of incorrect storage replacement. One failed headless click delivered an effect: never replay it. Later scenarios within failed cases and Mac modal follow-up are unexecuted. Protocol-headed9/10 fails despite zero observed residuals; healthy controls do not identify a causal fix.\n\nAll17 standard job logs saved, including a Mac invalid-ZIP retry. A premature count/projection failure is retained without false totals. Eight full lifetime comparisons remain recorded; native79's136/142 and older unknown ownership candidates are not retrospectively classified. No role/name/age/window exclusions or PID-hint kill/lease/debt authority. Current stable Playwright is still1.64.1; issue-search metadata provides no demonstrated cause or approved upgrade.\n\nExecution ledger/report keep G00–G18 incomplete. Historical missing evidence remains blocked while independent work continues. No artifact-download/auth/TLS bypass, privileged install, deadline raises, forced/replayed input, default transport/channel switch, merge or publication.\n",
